{
  "name": "Find work emails for LinkedIn profile URLs in Google Sheets with Apify (no cookies, pay per email)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 760,
        "content": "## Find work emails for LinkedIn profile URLs in Google Sheets\n\n### Who's it for\nSales, recruiting and growth teams with a sheet of LinkedIn profile URLs (event attendees, Sales Navigator exports, a CRM list) who need an email address for each person without a LinkedIn login or a browser extension.\n\n### How it works\n1. Reads the `linkedinUrl` column of your Google Sheet.\n2. Collects the URLs into one list and runs **LinkedIn Email Finder** (`b2bsearch/linkedin-email-finder`) on Apify once for the whole list. The Actor reads addresses on record from a database of 800M+ professional profiles; it does not scrape LinkedIn pages.\n3. Keeps the rows where an address was found and appends them to a results sheet: email, email type (work or personal), name, title, company, profile URL.\n\n### Setup steps\n- Add your Apify credential to the Apify node (API token from Apify Console → Settings → Integrations).\n- Pick the input sheet (column `linkedinUrl`) in **Read profile URLs** and the output sheet in **Append emails**.\n- Optional: set `includePersonalEmails: true` in the Apify node body to also receive personal addresses.\n\n### Requirements\n- Apify account (free plan works). $8 per 1,000 profiles with an address found; profiles without an address are free rows. A list of 1,000 URLs finishes in a few minutes.\n- Google Sheets credential.\n\n### Disclosure\nThe Apify Actor in this template is built by the author of the template. It is pay per result: a miss is a free row."
      },
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -900,
        -220
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "width": 420,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "## 1. Read the list\nOne row per LinkedIn profile URL. Bare handles (`satyanadella`) work too. Up to 10,000 per run.",
        "color": 7
      },
      "name": "Note: read",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -380,
        -220
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "width": 420,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "## 2. One Actor run for the whole list\nThe Aggregate node turns the rows into one `profileUrls` array so the Actor runs once. Every output row carries `_status`: `found` is the paid result, `no_email` and `not_found` are free.",
        "color": 7
      },
      "name": "Note: apify",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
